    ],
    [
      "DIV",
      {
        "data-btype": "basic"
      },
      "On the AT chart, Algo3 emits 896 touch events (margin 0) and 1261 events (margin 30) that fall inside active NF regions. The cross-check confirms the independent validator and production `BlockAreas.blocked()` agree on all 17,308 events."
    ],
    [
      "DIV",
      {
        "data-btype": "basic"
      },
      "Attribution shows that the violations do not come from the NF-checked placement paths (`",
      [
        "SPAN",
        {
          "style": "font-style: italic"
        },
        "tap`, `"
      ],
      "flick`), which produce zero DOWN/MOVE violations. They come from paths that emit positions without any NF check: HOLD/DRAG continuation (`allocate` step 3), DRAG/HOLD onset (`",
      "_down` for type 2), and the UP of those pointers."
    ],
    [
      "DIV",
      {
        "data-btype": "basic"
      },
      "Root cause (source-confirmed): the NF check exists only in `",
      [
        "SPAN",
        {
          "style": "font-style: italic"
        },
        "tap` and `"
      ],
      "flick` placement. HOLD body positions, DRAG `",
      "_drag` positions, and `allocate` step 3 continuation MOVEs bypass it. `Frame.add` also clamps positions through `recalc",
      "_pos`, which is not NF-aware."
    ],
